@page
@model ErrorModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Something went wrong";
    Layout = "_PublicLayout";
}

@*
    Was the untouched scaffold page: Bootstrap's own classes (which is why the Bootstrap chassis had
    to stay vendored at all), and three paragraphs telling the visitor to set ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT
    to Development — advice aimed at a developer, shown to whoever actually hit the error, on a page
    that is reachable by anyone.

    Anyone can reach this page, signed in or not, so it stays on _PublicLayout and says nothing about
    the failure beyond the request id. The detail belongs in the logs.
*@

<div class="policy">
    <h1>Something went wrong</h1>
    <p>
        Sorry — that request could not be completed. The problem has been recorded, and nothing you
        entered has been lost unless you were told otherwise.
    </p>

    @if (Model.ShowRequestId)
    {
        <p>
            If you get in touch about this, quoting the reference below will let us find the exact
            request in the logs.
        </p>
        <p><strong>Reference:</strong> <code>@Model.RequestId</code></p>
    }

    <p><a href="/">Back to the start</a></p>
</div>
